            <ArticleTitle>A new method for coronary occlusion and local stabilization during minimally invasive LIMA-to-LAD-bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>206-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The minimally invasive direct coronary occlusion and stabilizing technique (midCOAST)-system, a new device for coronary occlusion and local stabilization during minimally invasive LIMA-to-LAD-bypass is presented. A closed platform with an oval opening in its center provides optimal immobilization together with platform-fixed vessel-loops, which are used for LAD-occlusion. Clinical results in 72 consecutive patients indicate that the midCOAST-device can be safely and effectively used for minimally invasive LIMA-to-LAD-procedure, even in patients with impaired left ventricular function. Due to the optimal immobilization of the target area the quality of the LIMA-to-LAD-anastomosis, documented by post-operative angiography (62/72), was excellent in all cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
